    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d858">

                <pb facs="0734" n="724" xml:id="pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.931/4–2549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-25T13:00:00-04:00">April 25, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>516. Urtel 856 Apr 25. You are instructed have MA<anchor n="3" xml:id="d858-f1"/>
                    immed approach highest available Commie mil auths Nanking and enter strong oral
                    protest against action Commie soldiers violating Ambs residence, indicating he
                    is doing so on instructions from his Govt. Suggest he might in ur discretion
                    support such protest with memo setting forth factual acct incident.</p>
                <p>Emb should follow up with approach to Commie civil auths when they are
                    established Nanking.</p>
                <p>Did Commie soldiers use threats or show of arms to compel Chi porter open
                    gate?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d858-f1" n="3" xml:id="d858-f1-content">
                <p>Military Attaché in China, Brig. Gen. Robert H. Soule</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
